Package: cellprogramsMC
Type: Package
Title: SEACells-Backed Metacells with mcRigor QC for Cell Programs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Mikhael Dito", "Manurung", email = "mikhael@example.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Constructs transcriptomically homogeneous metacells from a Seurat
    object using 'SEACells' (Persad et al. 2023, doi:10.1038/s41587-023-01716-9)
    as the aggregation backend, stratified by user-supplied groupings following
    the 'hdWGCNA' MetacellsByGroups interface (Morabito et al. 2023,
    doi:10.1016/j.crmeth.2023.100498). Metacell quality is governed by 'mcRigor'
    (Liu & Li 2025, doi:10.1038/s41467-025-63626-5): dubious-metacell detection
    via mcDiv double-permutation nulls, DubRate/ZeroRate scoring, and optional
    granularity optimization. Python dependencies are managed with 'basilisk'
    for reproducible R-Python interoperability. Output feeds cellprograms /
    cebmf_torch program discovery. SEACells is GPLv2 and mcRigor is MIT; both
    are used as external dependencies (isolated basilisk environment), never
    source-copied.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3)
Imports:
    basilisk,
    reticulate,
    Seurat,
    SeuratObject,
    Matrix,
    mcRigor,
